    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span><span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip bad\">Hard</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Binary search on the answer</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/split-array-largest-sum/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 410</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Split Array Largest Sum</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Do not search for the split, search for the cap: \"can I cut into at most k parts with every part ≤ cap?\" is a greedy O(n) check, and it flips from no to yes exactly once. Binary search the cap: O(n log(sum)) time, O(1) space.</p>\n"
